## Task
Emit **strict JSON only** — no surrounding prose, no Markdown code fence:

```json
{
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "file": "path/to/file",
      "line": 123,
      "type": "bug",
      "title": "one line on what to change (under 12 words)",
      "body": "how to change it, plus a brief why (under 75 words)",
      "patch": {
        "lang": "go",
        "before": "the original snippet",
        "after": "the rewritten snippet"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Field constraints:
- `type`: `bug` | `style` | `perf` | `security` | `concurrency`
- `title`: English, under 12 words, usable verbatim as the title of a GitHub PR review comment
- `body`: English, under 75 words
- `patch` **may be omitted or null** — when the suggestion is purely descriptive and rewrites no concrete code
- With nothing actionable to say, emit `{"suggestions": []}`

Principles:
- Every suggestion should paste straight into a GitHub PR review comment
- `patch.before` / `patch.after` are **code snippets**, not whole files
- Concentrate on how to change it; skip long rationales

Do not suggest (this avoids noise and dangerous rewrites):
- No destructive or semantics-changing rewrites: dropping error handling, swallowing exceptions, altering a public signature or default behavior.
- `patch.after` must be syntactically valid and behave the same as `before` — unless fixing a bug is the whole point of the suggestion.
- No pure style, rename, or add-a-comment suggestions that buy nothing.
- Nothing for files whose diff you were not given — with no diff there is no way to pin down a line number.

Example (shows the intended register only; do not copy the content):
```json
{"suggestions":[
  {"file":"api/server.go","line":88,"type":"concurrency","title":"Take the lock before writing conns","body":"s.conns is written from several goroutines, so guard it with s.mu or the runtime raises a concurrent map write panic","patch":{"lang":"go","before":"s.conns[id] = c","after":"s.mu.Lock()\ns.conns[id] = c\ns.mu.Unlock()"}}
]}
```
